\section{A row per student}

The command's unit is a student in an assignment.
It joins what FBF says (the progress, the breakdown, the grade sent) with
what Canvas says (the student and the score).
The score FBF computes, [[fbf_score]], is the overall grade scaled to the
assignment's points, the same scaling Canvas applies to the grade FBF
sends, so it compares directly with [[canvas_score]].

<<classes>>=
@dataclasses.dataclass
class Progress:
    """A student's FBF grade in an assignment, and what it is made of."""

    assignment: str
    points_possible: float
    student: str
    canvas_user_id: int
    fbf_actor_id: str = None
    progress: int = None
    overall: float = None
    fbf_score: float = None
    published: bool = False
    sent_grade: float = None
    sent_status: str = None
    canvas_score: float = None
    facets: list = dataclasses.field(default_factory=list)
@

Every Canvas student gets a row, also those who never opened the activity
and so have no progress in FBF: they are the ones a teacher may need to
remind.
Their FBF fields stay [[None]], which tells them from a student with
progress 0.
FBF users who are not students in Canvas---teachers, assistants, students
who dropped out---get no row, since Canvas has no grade of theirs to
explain.

The student is named by the Canvas login, which is what the other
[[canvaslms]] commands show, and the rows are sorted by it, ignoring case,
so that a login with capitals does not jump ahead of the others.
Of the arguments, [[scores]] maps Canvas user ids to their scores in the
assignment, and [[sent]] maps the ids of the grades sent to the
[[lti/grade]] resources.

<<functions>>=
def assemble(assignment, tasks, progresses, sent, student_of, students,
             scores):
    """Return the `Progress` of every Canvas student in `assignment`.

    `student_of` maps actor ids to students (see `match_actors`).
    """
    chosen = {}
    for resource in progresses:
        student = student_of.get(related_id(resource, "actor"))
        if student is not None and (
                student.id not in chosen
                or preference(resource) > preference(chosen[student.id][1])):
            chosen[student.id] = (student, resource)
    rows = {id: progress_row(assignment, resource, tasks, sent, student,
                             scores)
            for id, (student, resource) in chosen.items()}
    for student in students:
        if student.id not in rows:
            rows[student.id] = Progress(
                assignment=assignment.name,
                points_possible=assignment.points_possible,
                student=student_name(student), canvas_user_id=student.id,
                canvas_score=scores.get(student.id))
    return sorted(rows.values(), key=lambda row: row.student.lower())


def student_name(student):
    """Return the name we show for a Canvas `student`."""
    return (getattr(student, "login_id", None)
            or getattr(student, "email", None) or str(student.id))
@

A student can have more than one progress.
FBF knows people by two types, [[users]] and [[people]], and the same
address could belong to one of each.
Our course had no such student among its 180 students in 62 activities, but
if one came, letting the last progress win, as a plain dictionary would,
could replace a published grade by an empty [[people]] progress: the row
would show no grade sent, and the grade Canvas has as a mismatch.
The progress that matters is the one FBF graded from, so we prefer the one
with a grade sent, and otherwise the one with the higher overall grade.
The command notes how many progresses it set aside (\cref{progress-fetch}).

<<functions>>=
def preference(resource):
    """Sort key: which of a student's progresses explains the grade."""
    overall = (attribute(resource, "grades") or {}).get("overall") or 0
    return (related_id(resource, "latest-grade") is not None, overall)
@

The row of a student with progress fills in the FBF side.
A grade sent is optional: [[latest-grade]] is empty until FBF publishes.

<<functions>>=
def progress_row(assignment, resource, tasks, sent, student, scores):
    """Return the `Progress` of a student with a progress `resource`."""
    overall = (attribute(resource, "grades") or {}).get("overall") or 0
    points = assignment.points_possible
    grade = sent.get(related_id(resource, "latest-grade"))
    return Progress(
        assignment=assignment.name, points_possible=points,
        student=student_name(student), canvas_user_id=student.id,
        fbf_actor_id=related_id(resource, "actor"),
        progress=attribute(resource, "progress"),
        overall=overall,
        fbf_score=None if points is None else overall / 100 * points,
        published=bool(attribute(resource, "grades-published-at")),
        sent_grade=attribute(grade, "grade") if grade else None,
        sent_status=attribute(grade, "result-status") if grade else None,
        canvas_score=scores.get(student.id),
        facets=breakdown(resource, tasks))
@

